<title>POLAND: KGHM gives details on output increase.</title>
<headline>KGHM gives details on output increase.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish copper firm KGHM SA will increase production of electrolytic copper this year by 16,842 tonnes and copper in concentrate by 5,000 tonnes, in line with earlier forecasts, the firm said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It gave no other details. KGHM said in its recent issue prospectus that it would produce some 470,000 tonnes of copper this year.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
